repository-code: "https://github.com/rmonteiro-pereira/vit-vertebrae-pose"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-31"
keywords:
  - vision transformer
  - keypoint detection
  - medical imaging
  - pose estimation
  - benchmark
  - cervical spine
abstract: >-
  A controlled comparison of Vision Transformers for localising two cervical-spine
  landmarks in lateral videofluoroscopy frames. 169 archived training runs are
  aggregated into a nine-model by six-configuration grid, 48 of its 54 cells filled,
  with 95% confidence intervals and per-cell run traceability. Seven of the nine
  labels are the backbones the package ships; two are unverified builders, kept out
  of the model ranking and marked elsewhere. The strongest effect is that freezing
  the pretrained backbone degrades accuracy in all 23 comparable cells, by +36% to
  +558% (+36% to +280% across the seven shipped backbones alone). Model scale does not help: a 30.9M-parameter backbone matches or
  beats a 429.9M one. Augmentation changes sign by architecture. The study also
  reports its own noise floor, measured at 1.20 px between identically-weighted
  configurations, which exceeds the 1.12 px gap between the best cell and the
  baseline and therefore renders the ranking among fine-tuned configurations
  unresolvable at one seed per cell.
